  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Kim’s flight took off from Newark at \\(10{:}34\\) am and landed in Miami at \\(1{:}18\\) pm. Both cities are in the same time zone. If her flight took \\(h\\) hours and \\(m\\) minutes, with \\(0 \\le m \\lt 60,\\) what is \\(h + m?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(46\\)",
    "B": "\\(47\\)",
    "C": "\\(50\\)",
    "D": "\\(53\\)",
    "E": "\\(54\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Both cities use the same time zone, so we can compare the clock readings directly. From \\(10{:}34\\) am to \\(12{:}34\\) pm is \\(2\\) hours. From \\(12{:}34\\) pm to \\(1{:}18\\) pm is\n\\[\n(60-34)+18=44\n\\]\nminutes. Thus \\(h=2\\) and \\(m=44\\), which satisfies \\(0\\le m<60\\). Therefore\n\\[\nh+m=2+44=\\boxed{46},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
